1
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:03,100
"Kiss Or Kill"

2
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,000
(Episode 4)

3
00:01:19,959 --> 00:01:21,079
A little bigger.

4
00:01:21,319 --> 00:01:22,319
Slow down, slow down.

5
00:01:24,079 --> 00:01:25,280
Get up, get up.

6
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,400
Get up.

7
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:27,840
Get up.

8
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,400
Come on, be careful.

9
00:01:31,959 --> 00:01:32,959
Be careful.

10
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,680
Second Uncle.

11
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,518
A-ren, take the kids downstairs.

12
00:01:37,519 --> 00:01:38,519
Come on, follow me.

13
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:44,439
A-yan.

14
00:01:44,799 --> 00:01:46,519
I heard something happened at your place.

15
00:01:46,719 --> 00:01:47,920
I was worried sick.

16
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:49,879
But looking at it now,

17
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:51,879
it doesn't seem like a big deal.

18
00:01:52,079 --> 00:01:53,079
Thanks to Nie Chuan.

19
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,016
He spotted the assassins
sneaking in just in time

20
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,040
and saved my life.

21
00:01:57,439 --> 00:01:59,680
You mean the guide?

22
00:02:00,519 --> 00:02:01,079
Yes.

23
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,440
He's the one who saved me.

24
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,239
You really trust him.

25
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:05,840
I only trust the facts.

26
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,536
There's a shipment coming
up in the next couple of days.

27
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,575
I need you to make the run.

28
00:02:11,599 --> 00:02:13,080
Take him with you.

29
00:02:18,599 --> 00:02:19,599
Got it, Second Uncle.

30
00:02:19,919 --> 00:02:20,919
A-yan.

31
00:02:21,039 --> 00:02:22,120
Thanks for your hard work.

32
00:02:22,479 --> 00:02:24,079
Don't put too much pressure on yourself.

33
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,800
Otherwise,

34
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,800
my brother and sister-in-law will blame me.

35
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,400
Go on.

36
00:02:34,039 --> 00:02:35,039
Understood, Second Uncle.

37
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,680
Lin Yan.

38
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,680
What's up?

39
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,879
Do you really trust that guy so much?

40
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,520
When it comes to my business,

41
00:02:57,599 --> 00:02:58,960
I make my own judgments.

42
00:02:59,199 --> 00:03:00,879
What kind of judgment is that?

43
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:03,520
Are you really after his routes,

44
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:04,919
or are you after him?

45
00:03:06,759 --> 00:03:09,199
He did save my life, after all.

46
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,878
In all these years, when have you ever

47
00:03:10,879 --> 00:03:12,599
let an outsider into your home?

48
00:03:12,879 --> 00:03:14,800
You even used yourself as bait to test him.

49
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:17,840
You did it on purpose.

50
00:03:19,719 --> 00:03:20,919
Focus your smarts

51
00:03:21,439 --> 00:03:22,599
on real business.

52
00:03:23,719 --> 00:03:25,240
So I hit the nail on the head.

53
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,680
What's so special about this guy

54
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,120
that makes you
break all your old rules?

55
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,040
Do you really trust him that much?

56
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,280
You're overstepping your bounds.

57
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:41,360
Didn't you say

58
00:03:41,361 --> 00:03:43,199
you hate leaving things to luck?

59
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:46,680
There's a first time for everything.

60
00:04:53,959 --> 00:04:54,959
You're back.

61
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,079
You really made yourself at home.

62
00:05:02,199 --> 00:05:03,959
A workspace with a pool.

63
00:05:04,319 --> 00:05:05,319
Nice perks.

64
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:06,439
I'm very satisfied.

65
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,719
Put your clothes on.

66
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,079
What clothes?

67
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,920
First I got beaten up by your guys,

68
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,160
then I had to fight off
those amateur assassins.

69
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:15,439
Now,

70
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:18,079
I can only wait for you
to issue me a uniform.

71
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:26,240
Then I'll just wear whatever's available.

72
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,759
Your clothes fit me perfectly.

73
00:06:05,439 --> 00:06:06,518
Stop staring.

74
00:06:06,519 --> 00:06:08,399
Eat up while it's hot.

75
00:06:08,639 --> 00:06:09,560
I made it for you.
You made this?

76
00:06:12,439 --> 00:06:13,480
Who else?

77
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,399
Have you brought anyone else in here?

78
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,399
How is it? Not bad, right?

79
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,800
It's edible.

80
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,319
Edible?

81
00:06:26,959 --> 00:06:28,040
Then don't eat it.

82
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,279
I actually took lessons.

83
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,799
You learned how to cook?

84
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,400
I picked it up from wilderness survival.

85
00:06:37,759 --> 00:06:38,560
I couldn't just

86
00:06:38,561 --> 00:06:40,001
eat survival rations for every meal.

87
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,279
The ingredients in your fridge

88
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,399
are really top-notch.

89
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,719
When I'm out in the wild,

90
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,360
I never get to eat stuff this good.

91
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:47,480
Clean yourself up in a bit.

92
00:06:47,839 --> 00:06:48,639
You're coming with me.
Where to?

93
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,120
To work.

94
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,040
Nie Chuan.

95
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,240
It's pretty good.

96
00:07:04,959 --> 00:07:06,279
What else do you want to eat?

97
00:07:06,519 --> 00:07:07,799
You can order whatever you want.

98
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:42,319
Took you long enough.

99
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:43,360
What are you doing here?

100
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:45,399
Keeping an eye on you.

101
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,839
Second Uncle never trusts anyone.

102
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,680
We came all this way

103
00:08:16,399 --> 00:08:17,759
just to pick up this little thing?

104
00:08:17,959 --> 00:08:19,120
What do you know?

105
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,935
The buyer needs to
receive the sample first.

106
00:08:23,959 --> 00:08:26,159
We only ship the goods
once they confirm it's all good.

107
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,000
And it takes two groups
to pick up a sample?

108
00:08:28,079 --> 00:08:29,079
Quite the production.

109
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:30,560
Do you know what

110
00:08:30,561 --> 00:08:31,761
dual-password verification is?

111
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:32,879
It's to prevent people like you.
People like me?

112
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,399
You're pretty cocky.

113
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,000
Hit me.
What are you looking at?

114
00:08:38,759 --> 00:08:39,759
Hit me.

115
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,398
Don't think I won't beat you up.

116
00:08:41,399 --> 00:08:42,399
You punk.

117
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:44,719
You drive, you pick the route.

118
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:45,720
Fine.

119
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:49,158
This buddy of yours

120
00:08:49,159 --> 00:08:50,519
has no filter.

121
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:52,399
Get in.

122
00:08:54,159 --> 00:08:55,639
You really treat me like a chauffeur.

123
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,559
You sit in the front.

124
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:57,639
It's cramped up front.

125
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,200
How is it cramped?

126
00:09:00,399 --> 00:09:01,639
Isn't that how you got here?

127
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,200
I have long legs.

128
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,440
Do you know the rules?

129
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,839
Why so many rules?

130
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,360
What gives you the right
to sit next to my brother?

131
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,360
Get over here.

132
00:09:11,399 --> 00:09:14,639
I don't think he minds.

133
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,080
Get in.

134
00:09:18,879 --> 00:09:21,440
Did you hear? Get in.

135
00:09:38,639 --> 00:09:39,639
Open the trunk.

136
00:09:39,679 --> 00:09:40,679
Stop the car.

137
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:43,600
There's a checkpoint.

138
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:47,720
Under the seats,
check carefully.

139
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:51,079
I knew it wouldn't be this easy.

140
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,398
I've driven this road for over a decade,

141
00:09:52,399 --> 00:09:53,360
and there's never been a checkpoint.
The day you show up,

142
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,158
Are you trying to say

143
00:09:56,159 --> 00:09:57,320
I leaked the info?

144
00:09:57,879 --> 00:09:59,039
You picked the route.

145
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,360
Am I supposed to be clairvoyant?

146
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,240
What do we do now?

147
00:10:03,759 --> 00:10:04,999
We'll just have to ram through.

148
00:10:07,399 --> 00:10:08,480
And then what?

149
00:10:08,759 --> 00:10:09,959
What do you mean, 'then what'?

150
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,758
If you ram through and shots are fired,

151
00:10:11,759 --> 00:10:12,999
we'll be completely surrounded.

152
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,278
What about the goods

153
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:15,360
in the car?

154
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,080
Then what do you suggest?

155
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,320
Look.

156
00:10:19,879 --> 00:10:21,758
They're only checking plates and trunks.

157
00:10:21,759 --> 00:10:22,759
Not the people.

158
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:23,960
Go on.

159
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:27,039
So we separate the car and the goods.

160
00:10:27,879 --> 00:10:30,119
Lin Yan and I will take the
goods through the backroads.

161
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,960
You drive the empty
car and make a run for it.

162
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:35,279
Why should I be the decoy?

163
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,919
Because you know this road best.

164
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,080
And they definitely recognize this car.

165
00:10:40,759 --> 00:10:42,200
You drive east,

166
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,680
and they'll most likely chase you.

167
00:10:44,159 --> 00:10:45,319
Lin Yan and I

168
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,760
will take the goods and detour
through the west factory area.

169
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,519
We'll meet up at Hongling Road.

170
00:10:50,679 --> 00:10:51,840
What if they don't chase me?

171
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,080
Even better.

172
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:55,080
Just drive straight to
Hongling Road and wait.

173
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,879
His plan works.

174
00:10:58,159 --> 00:10:59,239
If I lure them away

175
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,375
and you get away with the goods,

176
00:11:00,399 --> 00:11:01,519
who gets the credit?

177
00:11:03,279 --> 00:11:04,480
You do, of course.

178
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:07,056
If the goods arrive, it's
because you lured them away.

179
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,200
If the goods are lost,

180
00:11:08,559 --> 00:11:09,679
we all die together.

181
00:11:13,399 --> 00:11:14,519
Fine. Let's do it.

182
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,015
If you try to screw me over,

183
00:11:33,039 --> 00:11:34,039
I'll kill you.

184
00:11:34,759 --> 00:11:36,759
Then you better pray nothing happens to me.

185
00:11:48,759 --> 00:11:49,559
Gunshots.

186
00:11:49,679 --> 00:11:50,679
Let's go provide backup.

187
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,600
Go.

188
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,120
Right up ahead.

189
00:11:56,039 --> 00:11:57,039
Someone's coming.

190
00:12:20,399 --> 00:12:21,399
Watch out!

191
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,200
You're hurt.

192
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,440
Cut the crap. Let's go.

193
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,360
Ouch!

194
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:24,720
I haven't even touched you yet.

195
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:27,038
I pulled something while running.

196
00:13:27,039 --> 00:13:28,039
My arm almost snapped off.

197
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,119
Your arm's about to fall off.

198
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,240
Yet you still ran that fast.

199
00:13:30,679 --> 00:13:31,799
Survival instinct.

200
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,480
If I didn't stick close to you,

201
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,559
what if you just left me behind?

202
00:13:37,759 --> 00:13:38,759
Suck it up.

203
00:13:50,799 --> 00:13:51,799
Wait a sec.

204
00:13:52,639 --> 00:13:54,039
You're just pouring it straight on?

205
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,279
It's all we've got.

206
00:13:57,639 --> 00:13:58,759
Go easy, then.

207
00:13:58,919 --> 00:14:00,039
I really can't handle pain.

208
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:02,919
You're a grown man.

209
00:14:03,039 --> 00:14:03,799
Afraid of a little pain?

210
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,696
I wouldn't dare cry about
it in front of anyone else.

211
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:06,799
Only with you.

212
00:14:17,879 --> 00:14:19,080
The more you cooperate,

213
00:14:19,279 --> 00:14:20,440
the less it'll hurt.

214
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,320
Hold still.

215
00:14:22,639 --> 00:14:23,840
The more you cooperate,

216
00:14:24,679 --> 00:14:26,039
the less it'll hurt.

217
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,320
Did you do that on purpose?

218
00:15:06,399 --> 00:15:07,399
Yeah.

219
00:15:08,799 --> 00:15:10,320
I can't believe you admitted it.

220
00:15:38,639 --> 00:15:39,639
Move!

221
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,120
Hurry!

222
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,559
Not a bad wrap job.

223
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:01,759
Guess it doesn't hurt anymore.

224
00:16:01,879 --> 00:16:02,879
I'm serious.

225
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,240
A little worse than mine,

226
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:05,879
but it's decent enough.

227
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,080
Don't flatter yourself.

228
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:12,519
Just complimenting you while I'm at it.

229
00:16:14,399 --> 00:16:15,440
You were faking it.

230
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,200
Faking what?

231
00:16:18,159 --> 00:16:19,200
Three years ago,

232
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,560
when you were getting stitches,

233
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:22,200
you didn't even blink.

234
00:16:23,759 --> 00:16:25,879
Now, over a tiny scratch,

235
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:27,880
you're howling like you took a bullet.

236
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:29,759
You're as smart as ever.

237
00:16:32,159 --> 00:16:33,159
Nie Chuan.

238
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:34,799
I...

239
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:35,920
You guys, search over there.

240
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:36,600
Got it.

241
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:37,840
Follow me.

242
00:16:40,759 --> 00:16:41,759
Come with me.

243
00:16:58,759 --> 00:16:59,759
Don't fall asleep.

244
00:17:03,519 --> 00:17:04,680
It's not that cramped.

245
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:06,320
You don't need to be so close to me.

246
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:08,000
I'm just doing this for our safety.

247
00:17:18,119 --> 00:17:19,119
Ouch.

248
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,440
I'm still injured.

249
00:17:23,079 --> 00:17:24,079
They're here.

250
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:29,318
They shouldn't stick around for long.

251
00:17:29,319 --> 00:17:29,880
Nobody here.

252
00:17:30,079 --> 00:17:31,079
Look closer.

253
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,200
I thought I heard something.
If we get spotted,

254
00:17:34,359 --> 00:17:35,680
I'll draw them away.

255
00:17:36,359 --> 00:17:37,680
You grab the stuff and run.

256
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,160
No way.

257
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:48,160
Trust me.

258
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,159
I told you,

259
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,680
there's no way anyone could hide here.

260
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:08,599
It's clear. Let's go.

261
00:18:18,359 --> 00:18:20,119
Let go.

262
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,440
We're safe now.

263
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:30,799
Shouldn't we do something?

264
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,039
Get out.

265
00:18:46,079 --> 00:18:47,079
Let me see the wound.

266
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,240
It's fine.

267
00:19:10,241 --> 00:19:11,279
It's just a scratch.

268
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:13,720
Is this the real you?

269
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:16,240
So, do you prefer

270
00:19:16,241 --> 00:19:17,321
me faking the pain earlier,

271
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,440
or me right now?

272
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,360
Given the current situation,

273
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,480
we won't be able to leave
anytime soon.

274
00:19:27,039 --> 00:19:28,559
Luckily, they just searched this area.

275
00:19:28,759 --> 00:19:29,839
We should be safe for now.

276
00:19:30,039 --> 00:19:31,359
Then let's

277
00:19:31,599 --> 00:19:32,680
rest up right here.

278
00:19:35,759 --> 00:19:36,759
Alright.

279
00:19:37,039 --> 00:19:38,319
Let's set up camp here.

280
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:40,518
Then the task of gathering firewood

281
00:19:40,519 --> 00:19:41,559
is all yours.

282
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:42,880
Me?

283
00:19:56,559 --> 00:19:57,759
We can't leave tonight anyway,

284
00:19:57,839 --> 00:19:59,199
so we might as well get some rest.

285
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,680
Overthinking won't help.

286
00:20:04,559 --> 00:20:05,359
What's wrong?

287
00:20:05,559 --> 00:20:07,239
Are you still thinking about someone else?

288
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,720
Black Scorpion can handle it.

289
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,160
I trust him.

290
00:20:10,839 --> 00:20:12,358
He said you trust me.

291
00:20:12,359 --> 00:20:13,559
You say you trust him.

292
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:15,600
So who do you actually trust more?

293
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:19,839
I suggest you talk less

294
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:21,160
and save your energy.

295
00:21:00,279 --> 00:21:02,440
Going to the bathroom? Let's go together.

296
00:21:04,079 --> 00:21:06,159
Pack up. It's time to go.

297
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:07,160
So soon?

298
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,400
It's almost dawn.

299
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:13,559
Feels like I slept for less than an hour.

300
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,359
Don't you know

301
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,559
what it means to sleep with one eye open?

302
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,039
I really don't.

303
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:25,960
Why don't you teach me?

304
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:31,720
Who's there?

305
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:33,960
Stop hiding.

306
00:21:34,119 --> 00:21:35,400
I can already see you.

307
00:21:39,119 --> 00:21:40,119
Whose kid is this?

308
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:45,880
I... I don't mean any harm.

309
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,960
I'm just so hungry.

310
00:21:52,759 --> 00:21:53,759
Here.
